  "$verified_imports_note": "Identifiers the agent corpus imports, each confirmed present in the named version's type definitions. Populated by `npm run api:refresh -- --write`, which needs network access and is therefore a maintenance command, never part of `npm test`. Libraries absent from this map are UNVERIFIED, not verified-absent — the guard skips them rather than guessing.",
  "$export_surfaces_note": [
    "COMPLETE value-export surfaces, as opposed to the spot-checks in",
    "`verified_imports`. The difference matters: a spot-check proves presence and",
    "says nothing about absence, so it can never justify a failure. A complete",
    "surface can — if a name is not in this list, the package does not export it.",
    "",
    "Used by the trigger guard in scripts/test.mjs. A trigger string is an",
    "identifier claim exactly like an import is, and nothing checked them until",
    "`registerdevicefornotifications` (the real API is",
    "`registerDeviceForRemoteMessages`) and `tobeintthedocument` (a jest-dom",
    "matcher that RNTL does not have; RNTL's is `toBeOnTheScreen`) shipped in the",
    "very commit that fixed routing recall.",
    "",
    "`exports_ref` points at a list stored elsewhere in this file rather than",
    "copying it, so there is one place to update when a version moves.",
    "Type-only exports are deliberately absent: a trigger matches source text at",
    "a call site, and types do not appear there."
  ],
